    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-052 — GTK viewport height threading.** One commit. **Docs follow after merge.**\n\nCloses ADR-051's Deferred item: \"GTK allocated height threading to `render_pipeline`.\"\n\n## The definitive verification\n\n`HONEYBEE_LOG=layout ./build/bin/honeybee` on Wikipedia HTML article:\n\n```\n[honeybee][layout][info] layout: viewport=0x0      ← first render (pre-allocation, expected)\n[honeybee][layout][info] layout: viewport=1024x678 ← second render (real viewport) ✅\n```\n\n**`viewport_h = 678`** — that's `m_scroll_window.get_height()`, the actual allocated visible viewport height.\n\n**Before ADR-052**: same log showed `viewport=1024x0`.\n\n**After ADR-052**: `viewport=1024x678`.\n\nThat's the proof — `viewport_h` is nonzero in production for the first time, flowing all the way through `LengthContext.viewport_h`.\n\n## What shipped\n\n`m_scroll_window.get_height()` — the **visible viewport height** — now flows through:\n\n- `render()`, `render_with_css()`, `relayout()` — 3 signature extensions with `viewport_height = 0.0f` (default protects ~15 test callers)\n- `render_pipeline.cpp` forwards through to `layout_with_pseudo(..., viewport_height)` — the call site ADR-051 prepared\n- `window.cpp`: `on_draw` reads `m_scroll_window.get_height()`, tracks `m_last_height`, relayouts on **either** width or height change (was width-only)\n- `render_html` / `render_with_preparsed_doc` pass `get_height()` alongside `get_width()`\n- `window.hpp`: `int m_last_height = -1;`\n\n## The critical widget distinction\n\n```\nHoneyBeeWindow\n  └─ m_scroll_window (Gtk::ScrolledWindow)     ← visible viewport (~678px here)\n      └─ m_drawing_area (Gtk::DrawingArea)     ← content canvas (~60,000px on Wikipedia)\n```\n\n`m_drawing_area.get_height()` = content height. Feeding that to `LengthContext.viewport_h` would make `100vh = 60000` — catastrophically wrong.\n\n`m_scroll_window.get_height()` = visible viewport. This is what CSS `vh` actually means.\n\n## GTK4 API note\n\n`Widget::get_height()` IS the allocated height in GTK4 (`get_allocated_height()` was removed in the GTK3→GTK4 transition). So `m_scroll_window.get_height()` returns what we need.\n\n## Honest delta framing\n\n**Zero visible PNG delta.** Even with correct height threaded:\n\n1. `vh` feeds only `max-height`/`max-width` (7 renderable rules from ADR-051)\n2. Layout doesn't read either (deferred to min/max clamp ADR)\n3. `.vector-sticky-pinned-container` still `h=0` from ancestor culling\n\n**What changes**:\n- `parse_length(\"calc(100vh - 48px)\")` returns `window_height - 48` in production (630 at this 678px window, was -48)\n- Lands in `ComputedStyle.max-height` — correct semantically\n- Layout ignores it (no min/max clamp yet)\n\n**Same category as ADR-047/048**: correct infrastructure shipped before its consumer.\n\n## Test count\n\n- 644 cases / 2465 assertions unchanged (default `viewport_height=0.0f` protects all existing test callers)\n\n## What this delivers\n\n- **ADR-051's Deferred item closed**\n- **Correct `vh` semantics in production for the first time** (verified via log)\n- **One fewer prerequisite** on the sticky sidebar chain — the max-height clamp ADR now finds `viewport_h` already correct\n\nRefs #237\n",
